 "response": "**Sukukre's budget is now $1287K.**\n\n**Which records count**\n- Only Finance Office budget records were applied. Messages from Operations, Engineering, Legal, Sales, Marketing, PMO, Vendor and Facilities were ignored under the policy.\n- Finance Office notices about room changes, audits, cost centers, receipts and invoices do not change the budget, so they were also ignored.\n\n**How withdrawals were handled**\nEach withdrawal chain was traced to its last link. A withdrawal counts only if nothing later withdraws it.\n- **#0008 is void.** #1138 withdraws #0939, which reinstates #0128. #0128 then voids #0026, which reinstates #0011, and #0011 voids #0008.\n- **#0298 is void.** The chain #1088 \u2192 #1050 \u2192 #0813 \u2192 #0787 \u2192 #0540 \u2192 #0359 \u2192 #0317 ends with #0317 voiding #0298.\n- **#0017 still counts.** #1362 voids #0836, which reinstates #0282, and #0282 voids #0270.\n- **Other updates that still count:** #0061, #0018, #0216, #0247, #0411, #0455, #0526, #0653, #0641, #1217, #1302 and #0982.\n- **Updates simply withdrawn:** #0119 (by #0820), #0192 (by #1496), #0275 (by #1430) and #0804 (by #1480).\n\n**Calculation**\nThe budget starts at $2130K, set by #0001. All remaining effective increases and decreases were then applied in record order through #1598, which ends at $1287K.\n\nThis is a single sequential pass through the records; I did not do a separate second recount.\n\nANSWER: $1287K",
